# Phase 2 & 3: Storefront UI & Design System

## Goal
Transform the static `Nutrexia_Template_Claude.html` into a fully modular, responsive Next.js storefront (Phase 2 & 3). This will act as the customer-facing frontend (`nutrexia.in`), replacing the current Next.js placeholder page.

## Proposed Architecture

Instead of one massive `page.tsx`, we will break the design into maintainable React components. We will use vanilla CSS with CSS variables (no Tailwind, per your previous preferences) to match the exact aesthetic of the HTML template.

### 1. Global Styles & Design System
#### [MODIFY] src/app/globals.css
- Port all CSS variables (`--pea`, `--gold`, etc.) from the HTML template.
- Add global resets, typography settings (Inter & Space Grotesk), and utility classes (`.wrap`, `.btn`, etc.).
- Add keyframe animations (`scroll`, `pulse`, `fadein`).

### 2. Layout Components (Appears on every page)
